This product's design draws on the following MIT-licensed projects. No source
was copied verbatim; the debts are architectural and are recorded here because
the ideas are the valuable part.

  silverstein/minutes (MIT), Mat Silverstein
    - perception engines exiled behind a process boundary with an NDJSON
      contract, so an incompatible dependency graph cannot reach the host
    - append-only voice samples with revoke-only mutation, and voice profiles
      scoped by embedding model id so vectors from different models are never
      compared
    - solo-enrollment quality gates (SNR, clipping, window consistency,
      minimum speech, minimum RMS) and their threshold values
    - late speaker attribution applied by append rather than in-place rewrite

  juanmc2005/diart (MIT), Juan Manuel Coria
    - streaming diarization design and its published embedding-model survey,
      which selected the ungated ECAPA path used here

  KmingLyu/real-time-speaker-diarization-asr (MIT)
    - incremental nearest-centroid speaker clustering with a new-cluster
      distance threshold

  Gr122lyBr/voicetag (MIT)
    - enrol-then-identify interface shape and per-segment confidence reporting

  moutons/whotalksitron (Apache-2.0)
    - per-context voiceprint enrollment scoping

Model weights carry their own terms, separate from the licenses above:

  speechbrain/spkrec-ecapa-voxceleb   Apache-2.0, not gated
  Systran/faster-whisper-small.en     MIT, not gated
  snakers4/silero-vad                 MIT, not gated

No gated Hugging Face model is required to run this tool. Adding pyannote
segmentation for overlap-aware diarization would introduce gated weights and
must be re-audited before any commercial distribution.
